    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26846" root="طفل" body-key="T">[
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَافِلَةٌ</span></b> , which Golius explains as meaning “ <i>i. q.</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَايِدَةٌ</span> et <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَيْرٌ</span>, utilitas, bonum, ” referring to the
KL as his authority, is evidently a mistake for
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَائِلٌ</span>, expl. as meaning <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَائِدَةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَيْرٌ</span> in my
copy of the KL, which does not mention <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَافِلَةٌ</span>
in any sense.]

